   "text": {
    "L1": "We use representative values to describe a set of data.",
    "L2": "The mean is the total divided by the number of values. It is the equal share after levelling out the total.",
    "L3": "The mean need not be one of the data values. For 4, 7, 10 and 11, the mean is 32 divided by 4, which is 8.",
    "L4": "The median is the middle value after putting the data in order. In 6, 7, 10, 12 and 15, the median is 10.",
    "L5": "The mode is the value that occurs most often. In these shoe sizes, the mode is 6 because it occurs three times.",
    "L6": "One extreme value pulls the mean a lot but hardly moves the median. Here, the median describes a typical salary better.",
    "L7": "So remember: mean uses the total, median uses the ordered middle, and mode uses the most frequent value."
   },
